Subject: [PATCH 06859/11362] [outer-loop] ARC g50t round-4: honest null,
 clone-selective socket routing found

Round-4 codex gpt-5.6-sol attempt on g50t stayed in-budget (557/600 calls)
and confirms round-3's L4 tongue mechanic exactly. New discovery: the
color-15 paired rail sockets are CLONE-SELECTIVE -- a live body entering
the upper socket at (26,38) stays there, but a replaying clone entering
the same socket and moving RIGHT gets rerouted to a different lower
socket at (26,50). Also confirms movement (not just any input) is the
usable replay clock, and ACTION5 after both clone slots are used clears
clones and rewinds to spawn WITHOUT restoring the level timer.

Honest null -- fresh-reset reproduction gate on a 154-action candidate
reached only level 3. No registry count change.

